            "_view_name": "TextareaView",
            "continuous_update": true,
            "description": "Hyperparameters Selection Explanation:",
            "description_tooltip": null,
            "disabled": false,
            "layout": "IPY_MODEL_9bdfa481f4994079b315c339f0c2d40b",
            "placeholder": "<student to fill this section>",
            "rows": null,
            "style": "IPY_MODEL_ba18ef15c4874ba3a375f1760e0853bc",
            "value": "In an ElasticNet regression model, the two key hyperparameters — alpha and l1_ratio — play a crucial role in controlling regularization to improve model performance and generalization.\n\nAlpha (regularization strength) controls how much regularization is applied to the model. We ue alpha to prevent overfitting on noisy data, and improve model generalization to unseen data.\n\nl1_ratio determines the mix of L1 (Lasso) and L2 (Ridge) regularization. We use l1_ratio to control feature selection (L1 helps remove irrelevant features), and stabilize the model when there’s multicollinearity (L2 helps spread weights)"
          }
        },
