            "layout": "IPY_MODEL_e8e1bde0eb60468898d1744d4c51bf78",
            "placeholder": "<student to fill this section>",
            "rows": null,
            "style": "IPY_MODEL_9823a77d455f4049a0b37ba214a53ec8",
            "value": "Base on the line charts, and RMSE, the ElasticNet model provides some insights that can inform rental pricing strategies for landlords and property management companies.\n\nThe rent prices follow an upward trend. However, the model just can predict good at the rent range from $400 to around $800, it cannot accurately predict when the rent prices increase higher this range. \n\nIn general, the rent prices will rise when the properties have more rooms, larger floor area. They also will increase over the month, it maybe that July is the begining month of the Spring semester, which leads to the increase in rental prices due to the demand of both domestic and international students. However, this is not a perfect model for prediction, we cannot accurately predict the rent prices in future. \n\nThe best RMSE of ElasticNet model is near the best RMSE of linear regression, we can consider the coefficients of linear regression to give prediction. "
          }
        },
